id: pm-rl-prefix
title: Train a history-prefix learner on the public tracker environment
description: "PR 84 acceptance scored 107/214 on meta-validation versus the completed-majority baseline 211/214, and 198/385 on final-test versus 384/385. All candidates retained the zero-weight seed checkpoint because inner fits were refused. Add a bounded learner that actually reads the normalized history prefix, such as the existing LM adapter, on the sealed repository-split tracker environment."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-18T07:43:41.188Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T07:54:22.789Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Train only on training repositories; preserve inner-held-out, meta-validation and final-test boundaries, fixed pre-approved budgets and unchanged promotion gate; report majority baselines, prediction diversity and final-test scores; demonstrate statistically supported improvement or explicitly report a null result without weakening the gate."
parent: pm-rl-apvf
comments[22]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T18:18:15.113Z",codex-agent,"Plan: measure four candidate targets on training repositories only, freeze the selected task and split rules, then fit a bounded hashed prefix learner through the existing reserved process contract. Keep the 0.95 confidence, ten-sample, 0.01 effect gate and release disabled. Retain explicit fit, rejection, diversity, baseline and final-test evidence; verify behavioural reverts and both isolated release gates before opening the PR."
  "2026-10-18T18:19:57.854Z",codex-agent,"Training-repository-only screening on the original sealed commits (1168 eligible items): next lifecycle {closed:959,in_progress:195,canceled:10,open:3,blocked:1}, majority 82.106%; reopened {false:1144,true:24}, 97.945%; item type {Issue:447,Task:295,Chore:270,Feature:142,Decision:9,Epic:5}, 38.271%; median time-to-close {fast:585,slow:583}, 50.086%. Select time-to-close for a bounded binary learner: elapsed time and lifecycle activity plausibly predict remaining duration. Freeze this selection before either outer holdout is scored. Final calibration and all four distributions will use fit items only, excluding inner-held-out items, with a fixed seeded event cut and original source pins."
  "2026-10-18T18:26:53.048Z",codex-agent,"Fit-only calibration on original sealed public commits: 943 fit / 225 inner-held-out / 214 meta-validation / 385 final-test items. Median remaining duration 47356 ms. Candidate distributions on 943 fit items: next lifecycle {closed:776,in_progress:155,canceled:9,open:2,blocked:1} (82.291% majority); reopened {false:926,true:17} (98.197%); item type {Issue:368,Task:240,Chore:214,Feature:111,Decision:6,Epic:4} (39.024%); selected time-to-close {fast:472,slow:471} (50.053%). Synthetic real-process recursion passed 7/7 tests. Five behavioural reverts, with tests retained, each failed: replace feature vector with zeros; return source instead of fitted parameters; expose post-cut events; omit target-balance refusal; disable positive binomial verdict. Restore passed 5/5 focused tests. Revert transcripts retained in runtime/revert-*.log. No evaluation criterion or source role changed."
  "2026-10-18T18:27:41.455Z",codex-agent,"First real acceptance attempt aborted operationally before completing candidate scoring: checkpoint + completion receipt + mirrored NDJSON event consumed 4195 staging bytes, exceeding the unchanged 4096 allowance. Keep the refusal and original receipts. Quantise fitted parameters to four decimal places to fit the declared storage budget; do not enlarge any approval or statistical gate. Restart acceptance with this fixed numerical representation. No target or recipe was chosen from held-out scores."
  "2026-10-18T18:31:36.816Z",codex-agent,"The completed diagnostic run exposed a correctness bug, also caught by the synthetic acceptance regression: inner fitted and seed policies shared the recipe digest as their generation id, causing a self-comparison refusal. This run is invalid improvement evidence. Inner comparisons now use distinct checkpoint identities; outer comparisons retain recipe identities. Promotion confidence, sample and effect thresholds are unchanged. Rerun exactly the same target, cut, split, bounds and seed without tuning after seeing either outer holdout."
  "2026-10-18T18:35:41.543Z",codex-agent,"Final behavioural revert proofs: 8/8 mutations failed with tests retained. Reverting checkpoint-vs-recipe inner identity fails the inner-comparison regression; reverting prefix completion validation fails trainer IO; allowing inner-held-out items into calibration fails snapshot-builder assertions; zeroing features, retaining source weights, exposing post-cut events, omitting target-balance refusal, and disabling the positive binomial verdict each fail their focused regression. Restored implementation passes 8/8 selected tests. The corrected real-process acceptance/gap/replay regression passes 1/1. Local strict health reports a global pm-github/CLI version skew (pinned host 2026.10.13 versus extension host 2026.10.18); no-extensions storage authority passes. Keep dependency pins unchanged and verify the final head from an isolated fresh clone."
  "2026-10-18T18:44:53.988Z",codex-agent,"Live evidence: npm run test:live completed on 25 verified PUBLIC/MIT original source commits, 1767 examples, in 125124.91358699999 ms. Five actual fits changed parameters and finished evaluated; zero inner/recipe promotions. Fit target fast472/slow471; inner104/121; meta74/140; final165/220. Inner fitted correct counts initial124, m1c0=121, m1c1=133, m2c0=115, m2c1=124 of225; best gain0.053333333333333344, lower bound -0.1277468687654159. Fitted fast/slow diversity111/114,0/225,26/199,166/59,3/222. All outer scores140/214 (majority140/214), gains0, bounds -0.21778781183411927; retained policies predict only slow. Final before/after220/385 equals majority220/385; paired tests against both fixed constants yield max p=1, wins/losses0/0 for matching constant, gain lower bound -0.13843052463687777, accuracy lower bound0.5090542065482301. No final-test advantage. Process use:5 steps,8986 wall ms,15905 staging bytes,382 CPU ms,0 tokens; max job storage3625/4096. Sanitized docs/prefix-live-evidence.json binds every example to public repo/commit/prefix digest and implementation file digests. Nine behavioural reverts fail; restored paired regression passes. Plain test:live now defaults to this task; original terminal-disposition remains explicitly selectable. Release approval variable is unset."
  "2026-10-18T18:57:06.358Z",codex-agent,"Implementation and live acceptance are reviewable in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/86 at source commit 3e9bd8fb36d13fcbd6358cf46a93cdd3b9f14641. Focused prefix suite passes11/11 with0 failures/skips; new explicit evaluated/promoted job-state and replay assertions pass1/1. Both independent fresh clones pass strict health with merge drivers under isolated HOME/Git identity. Isolated npm and Bun full release checks and the three-job CI matrix are in progress at unchanged four-metric/documented-surface thresholds; final receipts will be recorded in the linked PR. The initial non-isolated coverage diagnostic hit the pre-existing300000 ms HTTP receipt crash-drill timeout (related pm-rl-bi4v); it is missing gate evidence. No upstream CLI/SDK issue was filed. Global extension/pinned-host version skew affects normal-HOME health but is absent in both clean isolated clones. Greptile's expired trial, neutral and skipped reviewer checks are not review approval. Releasing the implementation claim for orchestrator review; keep the item in_progress and the PR unmerged, with release disabled."
  "2026-10-18T19:04:17.712Z",codex-agent,"CI correction: the first Node22 job passed639/639 tests,0 failures/skips and native100% lines/branches/functions, but the independent statement gate correctly refused99.98% (1/4586 blocks) in dataset.ts. Raw V8 comparison identifies the history-prefix builder's null-projection fallback: ordinary fixtures had only terminal histories, while real live data exercised this path. Add a committed synthetic open-only history and verify it is excluded from the new task. No learner, target, budget, gate or production code changes are needed. Reclaiming to add and verify this regression."
  "2026-10-18T19:07:50.466Z",codex-agent,"Coverage correction verified: the synthetic open-only item is omitted and the focused builder regression passes1/1. Removing only the null-projection fallback fails with TypeError on the retained test; restoration passes1/1. This is the tenth behavioural revert proof. Combined raw V8 witnesses now enter112/112 dataset.ts blocks; full release/CI evidence must still complete. Production files and the committed real-data implementation digests remain identical. npm run build:test passes. Releasing the test-correction claim for continued CI verification in PR86."
  "2026-10-18T20:01:30.406Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: unify lifecycle-prefix validation between projection and sealed reads. Empty projected prefixes are ineligible; unknown preterminal statuses refuse with dataset_unknown_status, matching terminal-disposition extraction. Add real-builder regressions and behavioral revert proofs. Track capacity expansion separately without implementing it; preserve budgets, gate and historical live evidence."
  "2026-10-18T20:02:48.895Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for review round 1: retained test command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"lifecycle prefix contract: empty\" test/prefix.test.ts fails with only prefix-data.ts and dataset.ts restored to ed3f79c (sealed empty prefix reaches dataset_prefix). The unknown variant fails because the expected dataset_unknown_status refusal is missing. Both exits are 1 with assertion failures, not compile errors. Restore production fix: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"lifecycle prefix contract\" test/prefix.test.ts passes 2/2. Shared validator also verifies reader refusals and rejects unknown statuses beyond the sampled cut before the first terminal transition. Typecheck and lint pass. Capacity follow-up pm-rl-a2zp is open under pm-rl-apvf; no capacity implementation or live rerun in this correction."
  "2026-10-18T20:03:39.981Z",codex-agent,"Review validation: real dataset regressions 2/2; existing dataset suite 7/7; all three linked pm test commands pass (5, 8 and 2 selected cases). Typecheck, lint, duplicate gate and documented-surface gate pass: 39 source files, 306 documented declarations. Full unchanged npm and Bun release gates are next, with CI identity isolation. Pinned CLI remains 2026.10.13; registry reports 2026.10.18, left unchanged by policy. Normal-environment health still hits the existing globally loaded extension host-version skew; verify tracked health in an isolated fresh clone."
  "2026-10-18T20:06:22.714Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary check extends the same unknown-status regression to imported events containing unknown then closed in one event, and unknown with no terminal event. Validate preterminal states before eligibility checks so these match terminal-disposition refusal too. The two regressions pass 2/2; reverting only production files to ed3f79c still fails each with assertions, restoring passes 2/2. A local npm gate started before this final correction was deliberately stopped and is not passing evidence; restart against the final snapshot. No statistical, learner, budget or threshold change."
  "2026-10-18T20:22:24.236Z",codex-agent,"Review acceptance on exact commit 123b585caea390243e3833bcfc58f42d5d082ad7: CI run 39161799627 passes npm run release:check on Node 22 and 26 and bun run release:check on Node 26, with identity-isolated HOME/Git settings and unchanged thresholds. Each job: 641 tests, 641 pass, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; 39 sources at statements/lines/branches/functions 100/100/100/100; 306 documented declarations. Strict tracked health and CodeQL pass. Downloaded all three job logs and checked counts/metrics. Redundant local full-gate runs were stopped only after complete CI receipts; no local full-gate pass is claimed. The local long HTTP crash drill passed in both runs (117239 and 118053 ms). Both new behavioral revert proofs remain recorded above. Capacity expansion is tracking only in pm-rl-a2zp. Existing normal-environment host-version skew remains; gh pr edit hit a deprecated Projects field, so PR description updates use REST with published-body verification. No upstream issue was filed; no review replies/resolutions or bot mentions. Original public live evidence remains historical and unchanged."
  "2026-10-20T07:05:46.075Z",codex-agent,"Continuation after merged prefix PR 86 and improver PR 88: preserve the existing bounded learner, sealed source pins, budgets, data roles and promotion gate. Add evaluator-only probability calibration and two-sided descriptive accuracy intervals, including rejected fits versus retained policies and training-frequency baselines. Reproduce the original prefix benchmark and the ledger-driven improver cycle with two CPU threads at nice priority 15; report explicit nulls, behavioral revert proof and unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Existing capacity and statistical-power follow-ups remain separate."
  "2026-10-20T07:11:45.433Z",codex-agent,"Diagnosis from the original immutable inner train receipts: scalar weights moved only from zero to -0.000512 through 0.022725. Expected held-out reward stayed 0.499979-0.501396 versus seed 0.5, less than the 0.01 effect even before uncertainty. All sampled candidate means (0.497875-0.49925) were below incumbent 0.500125, so evaluation_rejected was appropriate. The feature is a single hashed lifecycle signature, signed only by blocked state; the bounded one-step REINFORCE updates do not learn rich history. Original class counts: train completed1014/cancelled9; inner144/1; meta211/3; final384/1. Calibration and real reserved fit/replay regressions pass; all four linked pm tests pass (5/8/2/1 cases). No statistical gate or source role has changed."
  "2026-10-20T07:18:27.469Z",codex-agent,"Fresh sealed prefix run completed in 244924 ms with the same dataset digest, five candidate checkpoints and scores as the historical run. Best inner fit133/225 has descriptive two-sided 95% accuracy interval [0.500571,0.681651], Brier0.246047, logloss0.685232, ECE0.021214; its unchanged gain lower bound remains -0.127747. Retained final220/385 equals majority, interval [0.502213,0.640644], Brier0.25, logloss0.693147, ECE0.071429; no recipe promotes. Metrics do not recalibrate probabilities or feed the gate. The Node stdin SDK-import issue reproduced during evidence extraction is already tracked by pm-rl-stdin; using a supported entrypoint succeeded. No duplicate or upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-20T07:24:11.679Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: retaining the regressions, (1) replacing prefixProbability with constant0.5 fails the probability calibration case, (2) restoring only diagnoseImproverLearner from the base revision fails the real reserved-fit candidate-calibration assertion, (3) reverting only the improver receipt binding to schema2 fails the required old-receipt refusal. All three exit1 with AssertionError; exact restorations pass1/1 each. Commands: node --test --test-name-pattern='probability calibration' test/prefix.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern='reserved fits preserve' test/improver.test.ts; node --test --test-name-pattern='legacy improver receipts' test/improver.test.ts. The expanded real prefix process/replay regression passes1/1, including refusing old-schema adoption before any phase. All files restored byte-for-byte; no gate, allowance or historical record changed."
  "2026-10-20T07:29:10.644Z",codex-agent,"Fresh ledger-driven run: 3 generations,34/34 settled fits,8704 SGD updates,577722 ms elapsed,0 tokens. Development ledger grows2/4/6 outcomes; candidate proposal probabilities and ledger digests change, but all12 matched sampled configurations equal incumbent draws under the fixed seed. All outer gains0; unchanged gate refuses2 meta trackers versus min10, lower gain bound -2.701814 and tracker CI[0,1]. Final audit remains8/16 time-to-close and12/24 Issue type, each50%; descriptive item CIs[0.160475,0.839525] and[0.222779,0.777221], Brier0.25/logloss0.693147/ECE0 on balanced labels. Explicit null; no learned-policy or proposer promotion. New aggregate receipts include all phase hashes and separate rejected/retained calibration. A declaration-only return annotation fixes inferred inline type imports; measured and published evaluator JavaScript is byte-identical. Full release gates will run in fresh clones so earlier installed runtime declarations are excluded without changing any gate."
  "2026-10-20T07:42:31.322Z",codex-agent,"PR89 is open at source c639adb7ed5d330e948eba5ddc6c7e148ec15db6: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/89 . The PR merge checkout has an identical tree. Published diagnosis/results/revert-proof text is verified and contains no local paths; auto-merge is disabled. Fresh no-local clone strict health passes with merge drivers and isolated identity; root lint and changelog check pass. The unchanged npm/Bun full CI matrix is running. Historical terminal-disposition accuracy intervals are now also recorded descriptively, separate from the original sampled hard predictions. Completed live artifacts are archived outside authored source scope with raw receipts retained. No merge, release, threshold or dependency-pin change."
  "2026-10-20T07:54:20.192Z",codex-agent,"Full source acceptance on c639adb7ed5d330e948eba5ddc6c7e148ec15db6: CI run39387106691 passes unchanged npm run release:check on Node22 and26 and bun run release:check on Node26. Downloaded and independently checked all three complete logs: each655/655, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo; all44 authored sources at100% statements/lines/branches/functions;321 documented declarations. Lint, duplication, attestation, production audit, pack, changelog, strict tracked health and CodeQL pass. Fresh no-local clone strict health also passes with isolated identity and merge drivers. The redundant local suite was deliberately stopped after complete required CI receipts; no local full-gate pass is claimed. PR89 remains open with auto-merge disabled. Final handoff adds only historical accuracy intervals, documentation and append-only PM evidence; TypeScript, tests, budgets, source pins and thresholds match the tested source. Releasing for orchestrator review, keeping the item in_progress and not closed. Known pm-rl-stdin remains separate; no new upstream issue was filed. Capacity and independent-tracker power remain open limitations."
